#: src\introduction.md:3
msgid ""
"**kanade — 奏** is an endpoint management system for Windows fleets. It gives "
"an operator a single CLI / SPA to run scripts, install software, gather "
"inventory, and stream live perf data from hundreds of PCs at once. The "
"pieces:"
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:8 src\operations/undeploy.md:9
#: src\operations/undeploy.md:54
msgid "Component"
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:8
msgid "What it is"
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:10
msgid "**kanade-agent**"
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:10
msgid ""
"Service that runs on each managed PC. Subscribes to NATS, executes commands, "
"ships results."
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:11
msgid "**kanade-backend**"
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:11
msgid ""
"HTTP API + projector. Persists state, serves the SPA, exposes operator "
"endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:12
msgid "**kanade-client**"
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:12
msgid "Optional Tauri desktop app. End-user-facing surface."
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:13
msgid "**NATS server**"
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:13
msgid ""
"Message broker for command fan-out + result aggregation. The agent talks "
"NATS-only; the backend reads NATS too."
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:14
msgid "**kanade CLI**"
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:14
msgid "Operator-facing command line: publish binaries, fire jobs, query state."
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:16
msgid "This site covers two audiences:"
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:18
msgid ""
"**Operators** running a kanade fleet — how to update each component without "
"ssh-ing into endpoints (see [Agent-mediated "
"updates](./operations/agent-mediated-updates/index.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:21
msgid ""
"**Developers** writing PowerShell jobs the agent will execute — what works, "
"what doesn't, what changed in recent agent versions (see [Writing scripts "
"for the agent](./developing/writing-agent-scripts.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src\introduction.md:25
msgid ""
"The detailed protocol / on-wire spec lives at [Spec](./reference/spec.md) "
"(the legacy single-page document; will be split into chapters as the docs "
"site fills out)."
msgstr ""

